Examples for: Shop

Background:
  Remy is a Chef
  Sam is a Viewer

Example: A topping goes on a pizza before the order is closed
  Given Remy creates a pizza with name "Margherita"
  And Remy adds a topping to it with note "basil"
  When Remy closes it
  Then the order is closed
  And OrderClosed is announced

Example: The base form of the verb reads the same
  Given Remy create a pizza with name "Funghi"
  And Remy add a topping to it with note "mushroom"
  When Remy close it
  Then the order is closed

Example: A closed order cannot be closed again
  Given Remy creates a pizza with name "Quattro"
  And Remy closes it
  When Remy tries to close it
  Then it is refused because only an open order can be closed

Example: Only a chef puts a topping on
  Given Remy creates a pizza with name "Diavola"
  When <person> tries to add a topping to it with note "chili"
  Then it is refused because only a Chef may do it

  Where:
    | person |
    | Sam    |
